This only avoids materializing a full Java value array when the known logical value length cannot fit the remaining byte allowance. Iterator keys are still materialized before charging; this does not bound RocksDB native work/RSS, visitor/projection allocations, the legacy Message/PayloadReference/SourcePosition fields, the complete mutation envelope, or production policy assembly. No legacy row cap or compatibility behavior is selected. A2 remains `IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION`.
